An unofficial command-line interface for JetBrains YouTrack.

Environment:
  YTRACK_HOST         YouTrack service URL or host to use instead of the default host
  YTRACK_TOKEN        token to use instead of stored credentials (applies to the active host)
  YTRACK_DEBUG        set to 1 to log HTTP requests to stderr (credentials redacted)
  YTRACK_CONFIG_DIR   configuration directory (default ~/.config/ytrack)
  YTRACK_BROWSER      command used to open URLs
  YTRACK_EDITOR       editor for writing text (then GIT_EDITOR, VISUAL, EDITOR)
  YTRACK_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER  set to 1 to turn off the daily new-release notice
  NO_COLOR            disable color output (as do --no-color and TERM=dumb)

Exit codes:
  0 success, 1 failure (including usage errors), 2 cancelled, 4 authentication required

Usage:
  ytrack [command]

Examples:
  $ ytrack auth login
  $ ytrack issue list -q 'project: APP for: me #Unresolved'
  $ ytrack issue view APP-123 --comments
  $ ytrack work-item add APP-123 --duration 1h30m --text 'Code review'
  $ ytrack api /users/me --fields login,fullName
  $ ytrack api /issues --paginate --fields idReadable,summary --jq '.[].idReadable'

Available Commands:
  api         Make an authenticated YouTrack REST API request
  auth        Authenticate ytrack with YouTrack hosts
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  issue       Work with YouTrack issues
  skill       Print or install the ytrack agent skill
  upgrade     Upgrade ytrack to the latest release
  version     Show ytrack version information
  work-item   Track time spent on issues

Flags:
      --debug       Log HTTP requests to stderr with credentials redacted
  -h, --help        help for ytrack
      --host host   YouTrack host or service URL to use
      --no-color    Disable color output
  -v, --version     version for ytrack

Use "ytrack [command] --help" for more information about a command.
